  "comment": "Archives the nanoserver-base smoke test extracts with tar (issue 5). 'fixes' rows are failures of the Windows tar.exe recorded in windows-nano-demos; 'regression' rows already worked and must keep working. Zips are checked entry by entry against their central directory (path, size, SHA-256). The 7z is checked against tests/expected/<file>.json (path and size from its headers), because .NET can't read 7z. 'pipe' extracts with curl file:///... | tar -xf -, which is a real pipe.",
